{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares","id":781756,"title":"A Few Questions about Nightmares","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-07T11:03:35-08:00","id":781756,"title":"A Few Questions about Nightmares","content":"So I've been reading over the Nightmares section of the book, and I thought I'd raise a few questions and concerns here. I'm a bit worried about this stuff, actually. Some of the Nightmares seem a bit hilariously overpowered, but I admit that I could be wrong, and that I could be misreading this. It is my sincere hope that the final product will not suffer from these issues, and admittedly I have no idea if they are already fixed in the final product (I hope so!).<br /> <br /> So correct me if I am wrong, but as far as I'm able to determine, the limitations on Nightmares are as follows:<br /> - only one Nightmare can be active on the target at a time.<br /> - lacking special abilities, you can only target one person with a Nightmare at a time<br /> - the target must be able to see your eyes to be hit by a Nightmare<br /> <br /> 1. Is there any limit to the number of times per scene you can use a Nightmare?<br /> Granted, only one Nightmare can be active on one target at a time, but is there anything to stop me from hitting everyone in the scene with a nightmare individually?<br /> 'Behold, my True Form!' is a single action with an instant effect. Is it considered to still be affecting the target for the rest of the scene for the purposes of Nightmare-targeting rules? If not, is there anything stopping me from building a character with maxed out Presence, sitting at High Satiety, and just using it exclusively in combat to roll something in the area of 14 dice minus my opponent's Stamina for lethal damage every single action? It's going to be -2 or -3 most of the time. Let's assume we end up with 12 dice after Stamina. That's 4L.<br /> Or combining it with Fear is Contagious at the cost of two more dice (which translates to about 1 less damage, so 3L) to hit two targets with it every turn?<br /> <br /> 2. Do people eventually build up any kind of resistance to a specific nightmare if they have been hit with it multiple times over the course of a game?<br /> <br /> 3. Certain abilities and combinations of abilities seem mind-bogglingly powerful. Am I missing something here? Is this working as intended?<br /> By way of example, I offer up All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, and then used in combination with Limb From Limb. I am here limiting myself to the <b>normal </b>effects of these abilities. No Satiety expenditure. No High Satiety/Low Satiety effects. No exceptional successes. Just normal effects.<br /> <br /> All Your Teeth Are Falling Out gives a flat -2 penalty to all Physical traits (and removes any trait that depends on physical beauty) which also applies to derived Traits. As its standard effect. This is an ability that seems like it would be perfectly reasonable if it existed in Exalted, but in nWoD with its smaller distribution of starting attributes, I believe it to be hilariously overpowered. Because of the smaller distribution of starting attributes, even if the target has chosen Physical as their primary, I am still taking at least one of their physical attributes down to 0. Even just suffering a -2 to Strength, Dex, and Stamina is bad enough, but the fact that it applies to derived traits as well is really the thing that takes it over the top. It doesn't just give my opponent a -2 to affect me, it also gives me a +2 to affect my opponent (because it lowers their Defense by 2). It makes them less resilient against damage, AND it gives them a speed hit.<br /> <br /> Now combine that with the effects of the Limb from Limb Atavism, which, as its base effect, lets you automatically inflict Arm and Leg wracks every time you do damage to a target that exceeds the target's stamina. Most people are going to be hard pressed to have a Stamina higher than 4. Average for a player character is probably going to be 2 or 3. Okay. Now it's minus 2, taking it to either 0 (if it can be lowered to 0. Not sure about that) or 1 . Okay. Now, if I do any damage at all, I automatically do an arm or leg wrack. Limb From Limb just got way, WAY better, and because AYTAFO also penalizes Defense, it is also going to be easier to land those blows to inflict the effects of Limb from Limb.<br /> <br /> 4. Does the target know that the Beast has inflicted a Nightmare on him or her? Would there be any way for them to know this or reasonably figure this out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 12-07-2015, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T19:03:36-08:00","id":782012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares#post781756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been reading over the Nightmares section of the book, and I thought I'd raise a few questions and concerns here. I'm a bit worried about this stuff, actually. Some of the Nightmares seem a bit hilariously overpowered, but I admit that I could be wrong, and that I could be misreading this. It is my sincere hope that the final product will not suffer from these issues, and admittedly I have no idea if they are already fixed in the final product (I hope so!).<br /> <br /> So correct me if I am wrong, but as far as I'm able to determine, the limitations on Nightmares are as follows:<br /> - only one Nightmare can be active on the target at a time.<br /> - lacking special abilities, you can only target one person with a Nightmare at a time<br /> - the target must be able to see your eyes to be hit by a Nightmare<br /> <br /> 1. Is there any limit to the number of times per scene you can use a Nightmare?<br /> Granted, only one Nightmare can be active on one target at a time, but is there anything to stop me from hitting everyone in the scene with a nightmare individually?<br /> 'Behold, my True Form!' is a single action with an instant effect. Is it considered to still be affecting the target for the rest of the scene for the purposes of Nightmare-targeting rules? If not, is there anything stopping me from building a character with maxed out Presence, sitting at High Satiety, and just using it exclusively in combat to roll something in the area of 14 dice minus my opponent's Stamina for lethal damage every single action? It's going to be -2 or -3 most of the time. Let's assume we end up with 12 dice after Stamina. That's 4L.<br /> Or combining it with Fear is Contagious at the cost of two more dice (which translates to about 1 less damage, so 3L) to hit two targets with it every turn?<br /> <br /> 2. Do people eventually build up any kind of resistance to a specific nightmare if they have been hit with it multiple times over the course of a game?<br /> <br /> 3. Certain abilities and combinations of abilities seem mind-bogglingly powerful. Am I missing something here? Is this working as intended?<br /> By way of example, I offer up All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, and then used in combination with Limb From Limb. I am here limiting myself to the <b>normal </b>effects of these abilities. No Satiety expenditure. No High Satiety/Low Satiety effects. No exceptional successes. Just normal effects.<br /> <br /> All Your Teeth Are Falling Out gives a flat -2 penalty to all Physical traits (and removes any trait that depends on physical beauty) which also applies to derived Traits. As its standard effect. This is an ability that seems like it would be perfectly reasonable if it existed in Exalted, but in nWoD with its smaller distribution of starting attributes, I believe it to be hilariously overpowered. Because of the smaller distribution of starting attributes, even if the target has chosen Physical as their primary, I am still taking at least one of their physical attributes down to 0. Even just suffering a -2 to Strength, Dex, and Stamina is bad enough, but the fact that it applies to derived traits as well is really the thing that takes it over the top. It doesn't just give my opponent a -2 to affect me, it also gives me a +2 to affect my opponent (because it lowers their Defense by 2). It makes them less resilient against damage, AND it gives them a speed hit.<br /> <br /> Now combine that with the effects of the Limb from Limb Atavism, which, as its base effect, lets you automatically inflict Arm and Leg wracks every time you do damage to a target that exceeds the target's stamina. Most people are going to be hard pressed to have a Stamina higher than 4. Average for a player character is probably going to be 2 or 3. Okay. Now it's minus 2, taking it to either 0 (if it can be lowered to 0. Not sure about that) or 1 . Okay. Now, if I do any damage at all, I automatically do an arm or leg wrack. Limb From Limb just got way, WAY better, and because AYTAFO also penalizes Defense, it is also going to be easier to land those blows to inflict the effects of Limb from Limb.<br /> <br /> 4. Does the target know that the Beast has inflicted a Nightmare on him or her? Would there be any way for them to know this or reasonably figure this out?</div> </div> </div> </div>That combo is even nastier than that: Spend a point of Satiety to inflict aggravated damage with Limb from Limb, and now not only are you inflicting the tilts when you do any damage at all, but you're also <b>literally </b>ripping their limbs off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T19:32:39-08:00","id":782029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=782012#post782012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That combo is even nastier than that: Spend a point of Satiety to inflict aggravated damage with Limb from Limb, and now not only are you inflicting the tilts when you do any damage at all, but you're also <b>literally </b>ripping their limbs off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I will see your Satiety expenditure and I will raise you adding the effects of Monster From The Deep to this combo, which, by default, subtracts half your Lair (rounded up) from the Defense of whoever you attack. Where it really gets funny is with the full, as brutal as possible version of the combo, though. The full, as brutal as possible version of this will cost you 3 satiety. Very expensive, yes. And to reliably get it off, you need to start with reasonably high Satiety, but it's a hell of an 'I Win' button:<br /> <br /> Step 1: Apply &quot;All Your Teeth Are Falling Out&quot; to a target of your choice, and combo it with 'Fear is Contagious.' Spend a Satiety to make it contagious. Wait until all or as many of your targets as is reasonable have interacted with the initial victim and are thus afflicted by the nightmare.<br /> Step 2: Make your appearance on the scene. Ideally you should be placed as close to the middle of the group of your enemies as possible. Do your best.<br /> Step 3: Use the Satiety expenditure version of 'Monster From The Deep' to make a brawl attack against everyone within (Lair x2) yards of you. Everyone's Defense scores should be, bare minimum, at a -3 (which only matters against supernatural targets, who may attempt to Dodge the attack). Even though the Atavism is Reflexive and there is no mention made of this special attack not being Reflexive, we will assume that this is an Instant action and not a Reflexive action.<br /> Step 4: Spent a Satiety to make it all aggravated damage. Apply either an arm or leg wrack tilt to everyone you do damage to. Congratulations; you have just <b>amputated the limb of your choice from every single person in the room</b>.<br /> Step 5: ???<br /> Step 6: Profit!<br /> <br /> (I suppose if you *really* want to, you could also add in From The Shadows to deny even your supernatural enemies their Defense entirely, but that's just showing off.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 12-07-2015, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T20:58:54-08:00","id":782060,"title":"","content":"I showed a friend who's an old hand the normal effect of &quot;All Your Teeth Are Falling Out. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> t's not too bad for a mid tiered combat character or someone with non physical combat abilities, for a beginning character its's pretty much you're out of the fight though. Will make a trained hitman fight like a 5 year old or make a werewolf fight like a normal human boxer </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T13:35:11-08:00","id":782471,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Nightmares are ridiculous. Nothing new under the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:11:22-08:00","id":782488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares#post781756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- the target must be able to see your eyes to be hit by a Nightmare</div> </div> </div> </div> Or be touched.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Is there any limit to the number of times per scene you can use a Nightmare? </div> </div> </div> Nope. There's no limit for vampires using Dominate 1, Majesty 1/2, Nightmare 1, Obfuscate 1, or any other certain abilities either. Werewolves have plenty of abilities that don't rely on essence either, Mage allowed affinity Arcana to be used without cost, Demon has Embeds, and Changeling had catches (not sure of 2e, but 1e at least). Spammable powers is not a new thing to the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted, only one Nightmare can be active on one target at a time, but is there anything to stop me from hitting everyone in the scene with a nightmare individually </div> </div> </div> Sure. Its called the time and effort you'd need to put into it, the amount of attention you'd gather, and the heroes you'd attract. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Behold, my True Form!' is a single action with an instant effect. Is it considered to still be affecting the target for the rest of the scene for the purposes of Nightmare-targeting rules? If not, is there anything stopping me from building a character with maxed out Presence, sitting at High Satiety, and just using it exclusively in combat to roll something in the area of 14 dice minus my opponent's Stamina for lethal damage every single action? It's going to be -2 or -3 most of the time. Let's assume we end up with 12 dice after Stamina. That's 4L. </div> </div> </div> Nope, go ahead and do it. Because, frankly, 4L a turn is actually pretty weak in the new 2e system. Give me a fireaxe, and I'm doing a base 4L with a single success as well, no min-maxing required. Start throwing on things like Giant Strength, and we leave your BMTF in the dust. Also, things like Relentless Hunter and Unbreakable reduces magic the damage. Honeslty, there are more effective Nightmares for combat out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or combining it with Fear is Contagious at the cost of two more dice (which translates to about 1 less damage, so 3L) to hit two targets with it every turn? </div> </div> </div> Sure, but that's less damage, which is also absorbed by damage reducing abilities. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Do people eventually build up any kind of resistance to a specific nightmare if they have been hit with it multiple times over the course of a game? </div> </div> </div> Multiple attacks works as justification to raise resistance attributes. So, kind of, and not in the way you mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Certain abilities and combinations of abilities seem mind-bogglingly powerful. Am I missing something here? Is this working as intended?<br /> By way of example, I offer up All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, and then used in combination with Limb From Limb. I am here limiting myself to the <b>normal </b>effects of these abilities. No Satiety expenditure. No High Satiety/Low Satiety effects. No exceptional successes. Just normal effects. </div> </div> </div> Not that powerful a combo for several reasons. 1) Unbreakable and similar on other supernaturals heal/negate Tilts like that. 2) There are any number of ways to reach the target threshold necessary for sucessfully causing tilts (notably, Giant Strength), and 3) lots of ways to inflict those tilts without using magic powers and 2 turns of combat.<br /> <br /> Now, lets compare it to other abilities in other games. Compare to Dominate 1, which basically takes a character completely out of combat. Compare to The Look, which lets me kill anything that breathes just by locking gazes without a resistance roll or counting health levels. Compare to Echoing Death, which not only kills you after a bit of set up, but so erases you from reality everything you've done in the past few minutes/hour is erased from existance as well. Compare to Efficent Killer, a -merit- that spells instant death in a lot of cases. <br /> <br /> This combo is trivial compared to what other games can do in 2e. I suspect you're still thinking in terms of 1e power levels. 2e had an overall jump in ability, and a focus on brutal violence when it comes to a fight instead of D&amp;D-esk combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Does the target know that the Beast has inflicted a Nightmare on him or her? Would there be any way for them to know this or reasonably figure this out? </div> </div> </div> Depends on the context. For Behold My True Form? Absolutely - you're looking at the person when they use the power to scare the hell out of you so much you take damage. Same with You Must Obey - kind of obvious who's the bully in charge. Some might be less obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T07:34:56-08:00","id":783434,"title":"","content":"So this thread made me go back and reread the Nightmares section again and notice some things (which resulted in the formation of the hacks below). <br /> <br /> 1) Nightmares are hallucinations. Not sure why they would ever be resisted by Stamina.<br /> <b>** Hack #1:</b> Nightmares are always contested by Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance (unless they use a resisted roll, in which case subtract the victim's Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance). <br /> ---- Some may complain that this hits them with the nerf bat. Valid complaint (but see hack #2).<br /> <br /> 2) Most supernaturals add their Supernatural trait to their power rolls. This seems doubly appropriate for Beasts. Beasts with bigger Lairs are scarier.<br /> <b>** Hack #2:</b> Beasts add their dots in Lair to their Nightmare rolls.<br /> <br /> 3) The normal effect of All Your Teeth are Falling Out doesn't jive to well with the How to Make Kinship Nightmares several pages later. The suggestion in the latter section is that the normal effect be no more than a -2 penalty to dice pools. Subtracting 2 from all three physical traits does seem a little harsh. It's also a bit unclear to me what happens to poor people who have stats drop to zero. Do they die? Are they paralyzed (i.e., do they die?)? More to the point though, the way the fluff is written suggests that Nightmares are supposed to do stuff to the victims while they sleep (i.e. while they are in their Dream Form), but humans don't have physical traits in their dream forms so this Nightmare has zero effect while they sleep... I don't know about anyone else but that seems like a hell of problem for the utility of this power.<br /> <b>** Hack #3:</b> The normal effect of All Your Teeth are Falling Out is a -2 penalty to all physical dice pools. All of this Nightmare's effects also apply to &quot;physical&quot; tasks that take place in the primordial dream. For example, if a hapless mortal affected by this Nightmare while in Dream Form tries to hit the Beast while they are both in the Hive, that mortal suffers the -2 penalty to their attack roll, even though the pool is nominally based on his mental traits. What matters is the perception of physicality.<br /> <br /> 4) Behold My True Form seems to rely on biological processes to inflict damage (the victims die from fear). Since undead and entities that were never alive to start with don't have such biological processes it seems like it should be way less effective against them.<br /> <b>** Hack #4: </b>Undead beings (such as Vampires and Mummies) or beings that were never alive to start with (such as Prometheans) downgrade the damage from this Nightmare to bashing.<br /> <br /> 5) The duration rules seem a little funky. For instance, if you don't buff the duration of You Must Obey with something like You Can't Wake Up, it's difficult to see how you can benefit from the effects that come about from High Satiety.<br /> <b>** Hack #5: </b>Nightmare durations depend on if the victim is awake or asleep. When used against someone who is awake the duration is the longer of one scene or one hour (this lets powers like You Must Obey unfold over multiple scenes if necessary). When used against someone who is asleep, the duration is the shorter of one chapter or a number of hours equal to 10 - victim's Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance (with the base 10 - Stamina hours roughly equating to the victim's sleep cycle).<br /> ---- Yes, this makes Nightmares really mean against people who are stuck in Dream Form -- just like it should be for a power called &quot;Nightmare&quot;.<br /> <br /> 6) The way the You are Infected Nightmare reads is that it is hyper-effective against Vampires rather than inspired by them (since normal mortals usually don't drink one another's blood).<br /> <b>** Hack #6: </b>Rather than affecting anyone who has tasted her blood, this Nightmare affects anyone from whom she has drawn blood (be that by biting them, scratching them, punching them, or cutting them with a rusty razor blade). At High Satiety, anyone coming into contact with the initial victim is also affected by the &quot;another Nightmare&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T08:18:35-08:00","id":783449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Nightmares are hallucinations. Not sure why they would ever be resisted by Stamina.<br /> <b>** Hack #1:</b> Nightmares are always contested by Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance (unless they use a resisted roll, in which case subtract the victim's Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance). <br /> ---- Some may complain that this hits them with the nerf bat. Valid complaint (but see hack #2).</div> </div> </div> </div> They're astral-based attacks that very much have physical consequences. One power turns your body to stone. That's not a mere hallucination. Hells, later on, you make an argument that vampires and prommies should be immune to a power because they're all about shutting down biological processes. And you just tried to change it from having physical effects. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Most supernaturals add their Supernatural trait to their power rolls. This seems doubly appropriate for Beasts. Beasts with bigger Lairs are scarier.<br /> <b>** Hack #2:</b> Beasts add their dots in Lair to their Nightmare rolls. </div> </div> </div> The higher your Lair, the harder it is to maintain high Satiety. This is a deliberate duality. Nightmares are for the High Satiety, heavy crossover, Family Dinner socialites that deal heavily with other supernaturals. Low Satiety are the powers that key off Lair. There are a significant number of mechanics tied into this duality, including the fact you no longer use Lair to resist powers at High Satiety.<br /> <br /> <br /> Normally, I don't really care how people houserule their games. But I feel compelled to point out that these above two have significant issues with them, especially with hurting the themes of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T09:51:56-08:00","id":783492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783449#post783449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're astral-based attacks that very much have physical consequences. One power turns your body to stone. That's not a mere hallucination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but the Primordial Dream butts up against the part of the Astral whose regular hazards include &quot;you may be physically transformed due to the proximity of your soul and a concept-world-being that communicates through pain and hunger.&quot; It may not be a constant threat like the Ecstatic Wind, but the Dark Dream is still comprised significantly of settings that can literally physically swallow you whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T12:10:16-08:00","id":783566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783434#post783434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The normal effect of All Your Teeth are Falling Out doesn't jive to well with the How to Make Kinship Nightmares several pages later. The suggestion in the latter section is that the normal effect be no more than a -2 penalty to dice pools. Subtracting 2 from all three physical traits does seem a little harsh. It's also a bit unclear to me what happens to poor people who have stats drop to zero. Do they die? Are they paralyzed (i.e., do they die?)? More to the point though, the way the fluff is written suggests that Nightmares are supposed to do stuff to the victims while they sleep (i.e. while they are in their Dream Form), but humans don't have physical traits in their dream forms so this Nightmare has zero effect while they sleep... I don't know about anyone else but that seems like a hell of problem for the utility of this power.<br /> <b>** Hack #3:</b> The normal effect of All Your Teeth are Falling Out is a -2 penalty to all physical dice pools. All of this Nightmare's effects also apply to &quot;physical&quot; tasks that take place in the primordial dream. For example, if a hapless mortal affected by this Nightmare while in Dream Form tries to hit the Beast while they are both in the Hive, that mortal suffers the -2 penalty to their attack roll, even though the pool is nominally based on his mental traits. What matters is the perception of physicality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightmares can also trigger immediately, so no damage to the utility since you can just have them go off now if you need it. As I read it there are two ways to go about a sleep triggered Nightmare either the person suffers an actual nightmare while they sleep based on the Nightmare triggered, or it acts like the Kafka's &quot;The Metamorphosis&quot; and the sleep triggers it and the Nightmare is in play when the person wakes up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783434#post783434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) The duration rules seem a little funky. For instance, if you don't buff the duration of You Must Obey with something like You Can't Wake Up, it's difficult to see how you can benefit from the effects that come about from High Satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really I mean the biggest duration issue would be that scenes themselves are variable in length. Otherwise I just view it as you can't make someone do something long term that would be fire and forget with the Nightmare. I mean the high satiety form just means I don't have to walk someone through every bloody step of what I want them to do, I don't need it to last a whole day and if I do well Nightmares don't cost anything and there's no rule against hitting the person again. All it would mean is I end up as a horror following my prey around and every time they start to snap out of it I grab the reigns of their brain again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783434#post783434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) The way the You are Infected Nightmare reads is that it is hyper-effective against Vampires rather than inspired by them (since normal mortals usually don't drink one another's blood).<br /> <b>** Hack #6: </b>Rather than affecting anyone who has tasted her blood, this Nightmare affects anyone from whom she has drawn blood (be that by biting them, scratching them, punching them, or cutting them with a rusty razor blade). At High Satiety, anyone coming into contact with the initial victim is also affected by the &quot;another Nightmare&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was in another thread, but its already pointed out that Kinship Nightmares are basically designed to attack the things you learn them from. They aren't so much how does this person scare others, so much as what scares this person. You are Infected as you say is a dangerous power against vampires since they do consume blood and the idea that even a single drop of blood they've ingested makes them a target would be a serious problem for a vampire. Against normal people it becomes like slipping a poison to them all you need is to figure out how to slip a drop or two of your blood into something they'll consume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T12:22:00-08:00","id":783574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783449#post783449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're astral-based attacks that very much have physical consequences. One power turns your body to stone. That's not a mere hallucination. Hells, later on, you make an argument that vampires and prommies should be immune to a power because they're all about shutting down biological processes. And you just tried to change it from having physical effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is different from what the book says. See page 132. Probably we'll be agreeing to disagree that this hack affects the game negatively (or even muchly vis-a-vis themes) at all. Also with regarsds to your claim that I'm being inconsistent. Things that affect the mind, like fear, can have a biological effect; however, they are still affecting the mind. It makes sense to me that you contest/resist with your mind. YMMV but IMO, its a push mechanically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783449#post783449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The higher your Lair, the harder it is to maintain high Satiety. This is a deliberate duality. Nightmares are for the High Satiety, heavy crossover, Family Dinner socialites that deal heavily with other supernaturals. Low Satiety are the powers that key off Lair. There are a significant number of mechanics tied into this duality, including the fact you no longer use Lair to resist powers at High Satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me see if I understand correctly. Nightmares are for heavy crossover where Lair will be low? Is that the idea? So crossover actually breaks down when Lair becomes high? I get where you think you've found some type of thematic violation but this looks more like poorly written rules to me. It's probably the case that Lair and Satiety are too closely coupled but it's hard to say because in comparison to the other 2nd ed games (including the revised Demon) Beast still looks under-developed. This could be fixed with some content-driven editorial oversight where the authors are challenged to better demonstrate that mechanics and intentions are aligned. Hopefully Paradox will provide some of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783449#post783449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Normally, I don't really care how people houserule their games. But I feel compelled to point out that these above two have significant issues with them, especially with hurting the themes of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't agree that they hurt the themes of the game. (If anything, they improve them but YMMV.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":".  Sorry, that should be p 133. Was looking to high for the page number... 12-10-2015, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T12:23:04-08:00","id":783576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783492#post783492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only that, but the Primordial Dream butts up against the part of the Astral whose regular hazards include &quot;you may be physically transformed due to the proximity of your soul and a concept-world-being that communicates through pain and hunger.&quot; It may not be a constant threat like the Ecstatic Wind, but the Dark Dream is still comprised significantly of settings that can literally physically swallow you whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's not anywhere in the book. Maybe it could have been if they hadn't just copy and pasted the ephemeral rules for angels, ghosts, and spirits. So...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T12:33:34-08:00","id":783581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783566#post783566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really I mean the biggest duration issue would be that scenes themselves are variable in length. Otherwise I just view it as you can't make someone do something long term that would be fire and forget with the Nightmare. I mean the high satiety form just means I don't have to walk someone through every bloody step of what I want them to do, I don't need it to last a whole day and if I do well Nightmares don't cost anything and there's no rule against hitting the person again. All it would mean is I end up as a horror following my prey around and every time they start to snap out of it I grab the reigns of their brain again.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the concept of scene. If I have to go from an alley, taking the train, to someone else's apartment, it's pretty valid to call it three different scenes, especially if substantial things happen in each venue. So...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783566#post783566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was in another thread, but its already pointed out that Kinship Nightmares are basically designed to attack the things you learn them from. They aren't so much how does this person scare others, so much as what scares this person. You are Infected as you say is a dangerous power against vampires since they do consume blood and the idea that even a single drop of blood they've ingested makes them a target would be a serious problem for a vampire. Against normal people it becomes like slipping a poison to them all you need is to figure out how to slip a drop or two of your blood into something they'll consume.</div> </div> </div> </div>How was this a cross-over game again? Doesn't Hunter adequately cover this kind of theme? What was the reason Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and Changelings don't hunt Beasts for sport? YMMV but this is one of the downfalls of Beast -- it does not adequately foster a crossover play environment. Railroading characters into relationships against their will does not go over well at the table. I've said it in the past, the whole notion of Family and Kinship is underdeveloped. That was true in both of the previous drafts and since the final draft doesn't substantially differ from the 2nd draft, that remains true of the game on the whole.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, house rules are house rules and not all house rules work in all houses. It's not like you have to use any or all of the shared hacks. They're merely one provided solution to a perceived problem. As far as I know no one's saying that these hacks are gospel. They are merely hacks (and not unreasonable ones).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T13:27:49-08:00","id":783621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783576#post783576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's not anywhere in the book. Maybe it could have been if they hadn't just copy and pasted the ephemeral rules for angels, ghosts, and spirits. So...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called critical reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T14:15:12-08:00","id":783647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783621#post783621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called critical reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure this personal attack wasn't necessary. Also since I work with humanists day in day out, I'm more than happy to report, critical readings have more then one interpretation (if they didn't most of the humanist side of academia would be out of a job). The great thing about these games is the modular sandbox design, which among other things means there isn't one definitive &quot;right&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; way to play them or write hacks for them (or do just about anything else with them). I'm sorry that some folks don't like these hacks but they are what they are. Like everything else, they're totally optional. Don't see why that's such an issue (still a free country last I looked...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T14:23:41-08:00","id":783656,"title":"","content":"If you wanna call it a personal attack, flag it. It's right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T15:04:29-08:00","id":783688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783581#post783581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is the concept of scene. If I have to go from an alley, taking the train, to someone else's apartment, it's pretty valid to call it three different scenes, especially if substantial things happen in each venue. So...</div> </div> </div> </div> Meh in this one I don't see much of an issue. I don't think You Must Obey was meant to be a fire and forget the way a vampire's dominate discipline can be. The issue, from what you've presented, seems to be that if I hit someone with You Must Obey and give them an order that will take a while I have no assurance that they will finish. The thing there is if you gave Beasts that kind of power then they're stomping over other groups. I mean a Nightmare costs nothing to use unless the player chooses to throw satiety at it I can't think of any mind domination effects in other games that wouldn't be rendered almost pointless if a Beast could just dominate anyone they wanted and be guaranteed the order would be accomplished.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783581#post783581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How was this a cross-over game again? Doesn't Hunter adequately cover this kind of theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I mean as a Hunter your job is to find these things and end them. I believe another theme that shows up is where do you draw the line on when a supernatural has become enough of a threat to necessitate killing it and when or if you can institute a live and let live policy, but I will admit I'm not 100% on that one. The idea of the Kinship Nightmares basically being designed to work against the creature it was learned from is reasonable in a different form than you seem to be thinking. With Hunters its learn the weakness and kill them. Kinship Nightmares its more you know these people, they're your friends and family as a result if you really wanted to you know how to hurt them badly. Now obviously these are the people you care about, you wouldn't use it against them, however that knowledge can still be applied to harming others it just is less effective the more dissimilar they are from the origin point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783581#post783581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the reason Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and Changelings don't hunt Beasts for sport? YMMV but this is one of the downfalls of Beast -- it does not adequately foster a crossover play environment. Railroading characters into relationships against their will does not go over well at the table. I've said it in the past, the whole notion of Family and Kinship is underdeveloped. That was true in both of the previous drafts and since the final draft doesn't substantially differ from the 2nd draft, that remains true of the game on the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way does it railroad people into relationships against their will? The closest we get to that is that Thicker than Water allows Beasts a good first impression, so long as they haven't given the supernatural a reason to hate them already.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783581#post783581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, house rules are house rules and not all house rules work in all houses. It's not like you have to use any or all of the shared hacks. They're merely one provided solution to a perceived problem. As far as I know no one's saying that these hacks are gospel. They are merely hacks (and not unreasonable ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is we're pointing out is when you seem to be missing the point of a mechanic. Like let's look at your first two. You're argument is that Nightmares are hallucinations and therefore should never be contested with Stamina, except that Nightmares are explicitly pointed out as still being real to the person experiencing them. Or your argument that vampires, mummies, and prometheans should be resistant to Behold my True Form because they're dead and therefore stuff like being scared to death shouldn't work on them when again the book explicitly says it hits supernaturals the same even if they wouldn't normally be able to feel fear, dream, or the like. We argue because in a lot of these cases its like you're arguing to fix problems that aren't problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T18:24:47-08:00","id":783816,"title":"","content":"The real winner for nightmares in combat is the high satiety one that makes eople suffer fatigue as though they have been up for 24hrs per success. That's a -4 penalty to everything per success, and if you get more successes than the lower of the target's stamina or resolve, they are knocked unconscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T18:43:42-08:00","id":783824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783647#post783647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The great thing about these games is the modular sandbox design, which among other things means there isn't one definitive &quot;right&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; way to play them or write hacks for them (or do just about anything else with them). I'm sorry that some folks don't like these hacks but they are what they are. Like everything else, they're totally optional. Don't see why that's such an issue (still a free country last I looked...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you mention modularity, which is often accomplished by the same hacks you're complaining about. Golden rule, man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T20:20:35-08:00","id":783889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783576#post783576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's not anywhere in the book. Maybe it could have been if they hadn't just copy and pasted the ephemeral rules for angels, ghosts, and spirits. So...</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see how your failure to understand the incredibly straightforward concept of &quot;the Primordial Dream, i.e. the subset of reality that this gameline's PCs control some portion of and are at least halfway inside at all times, can and does regularly draw people into it physically as well as spiritually through the simple nature of how Horrors feed&quot; justifies using my post to beat at this particularly tired drum of yours for at least the third time in recent memory.<br /> <br /> The effects of the Anima Mundi on the human body as a consequence of its effects on the human soul are not in Beast because they're not a key concern for Beast except in crossovers with Mage, in which case (judging from discussion of the Amnion as astral Mage Armor) 2e will presumably mention at least the basics of what the Ecstatic Wind can do.<br /> <br /> Until that book comes out, though, all that needs be known about how Beast approaches the Astral at its base is that there's two layers to the collective human unconscious, both of which contain representations of real locations and one of which is a dangerous nightmarescape inhabited by monsters like the protagonists, who can and probably will physically bring people into the Lair or at least make aspects of the Lair physically real for long enough to have undeniable physical effects (neither of which uses a roll that relies on their Lair rating), which means it's not much of a jump for the powers that get stronger when you can control your Lair better to be more than just hallucinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-10-2015, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T21:26:45-08:00","id":783918,"title":"","content":"Unrelated and without getting specific, look forward to Brookshaw's story in the Beast Anthology, as far as the Anima Mundi goes. It's satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T01:17:01-08:00","id":783993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=782488#post782488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(lengthy explanation addressing my concerns)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, MCN. That was really helpful. Much appreciated.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T04:41:11-08:00","id":784057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me see if I understand correctly. Nightmares are for heavy crossover where Lair will be low? Is that the idea? So crossover actually breaks down when Lair becomes high? I get where you think you've found some type of thematic violation but this looks more like poorly written rules to me. It's probably the case that Lair and Satiety are too closely coupled but it's hard to say because in comparison to the other 2nd ed games (including the revised Demon) Beast still looks under-developed. This could be fixed with some content-driven editorial oversight where the authors are challenged to better demonstrate that mechanics and intentions are aligned. Hopefully Paradox will provide some of this. </div> </div> </div> No, you don't understand correctly. Yes, High Satiety is for heavier crossover, because it is driven towards it by mechanics. Gaining Kinship Nightmares, maintaining High Satiety easier through Family Dinner than Hunger, innate abilities like Mother's Kiss works better with High Satiety, and so on. No, it doesn't break down at Low Satiety, but you don't get rewarded for it. You get rewarded for feeding your Hunger more, building your Lair, working on Atavisms, pulling down your Lair for a boost in Power, and so on.<br /> <br /> Its a deliberate desgn decision that High Satiety and high Lairs are mutually opposed. Hells, you don't even use the Lair for resisting supernatural powers, at High Satiety. <i>By design.</i> Being High Satiety is like being a bit of a twisted Sookie Stackhouse, a human psychic that gets off on being around supernaturals. Its as much of a valid archetype for Beast as the dragon or kracken.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that you're calling the book under developed, and being insulting towards the writers, makes me think that the problem is that you either don't understand the game, or just don't like the design of the game. Possibly both. Neither of which justifies being insulting either. Your opinions are noted. Good day, I'm done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-11-2015, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:27:04-08:00","id":784186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=783824#post783824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny you mention modularity, which is often accomplished by the same hacks you're complaining about. Golden rule, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Missing it. I wrote hacks. Others are complaining.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:53:57-08:00","id":784203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=784057#post784057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, you don't understand correctly. Yes, High Satiety is for heavier crossover, because it is driven towards it by mechanics. Gaining Kinship Nightmares, maintaining High Satiety easier through Family Dinner than Hunger, innate abilities like Mother's Kiss works better with High Satiety, and so on. No, it doesn't break down at Low Satiety, but you don't get rewarded for it. You get rewarded for feeding your Hunger more, building your Lair, working on Atavisms, pulling down your Lair for a boost in Power, and so on.<br /> <br /> Its a deliberate desgn decision that High Satiety and high Lairs are mutually opposed. Hells, you don't even use the Lair for resisting supernatural powers, at High Satiety. <i>By design.</i> Being High Satiety is like being a bit of a twisted Sookie Stackhouse, a human psychic that gets off on being around supernaturals. Its as much of a valid archetype for Beast as the dragon or kracken.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think I understand fine. I just think it's weird to interpret this feature in the manner that you do. Larger Lairs consume more Satiety over smaller intervals of time. Using Nightmares can also use Satiety (but doesn't actually have to). I'm not actually seeing the &quot;opposition&quot;. They're not mutually exclusive forces. Having a bigger Lair simply means you are less likely to benefit from the High Satiety effect. But that also just means the player needs to plan on around using the power. Not sure how that figures into the addition of dots of Lair to the roll in a hack being somehow diametrically opposed to basic game concepts. If anything the hack provides a baited hook for players to pursue high risk, high reward growth rather than establishing some stock rinse and repeat Satiety maintenance strategy. And what this <i>ultimately </i>reflects is that you and I have different approaches to playing this game. But I wouldn't claim that either approach is the <i>right</i> or the <i>wrong</i> one. They are simply different takes on the same text.<br /> <br /> I have to say too, you might have gotten more mileage out of your arguments if you had argued that a better hack would be to add the character's current Satiety before any is spent for the Satiety Expenditure kicker effect. But you are so focused on the wrongness of these hacks...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=784057#post784057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the fact that you're calling the book under developed, and being insulting towards the writers, makes me think that the problem is that you either don't understand the game, or just don't like the design of the game. Possibly both. Neither of which justifies being insulting either. Your opinions are noted. Good day, I'm done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you consider my critique insulting. It's a bit of constructive criticism to the design team. The book has failings. It has them because it tries to tackle a lot very hard to do themes (maybe too many of them). It's still better than some of the things from earlier editions (I'm still looking at you Geist 1.0). The problem I have is when someone acts as though customization is some high crime against the authors. It isn't. Sometimes the cracks they leave are on purpose, allowing for a multitude of interpretations and sometimes they occur because things in the development process broke down. It's hard to say what the cause was. I'm just pointing out the effect and proposing how it could be solved (in the future). It's fine if YMV but you might want to take a gander at the errata thread. As I recall there's something about the chapter describing heroes being (possibly) the wrong one. If that's the case then it seems like something broke down in the QC chain somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 12-11-2015, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T10:17:27-08:00","id":784231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=784203#post784203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say too, you might have gotten more mileage out of your arguments if you had argued that a better hack would be to add the character's current Satiety before any is spent for the Satiety Expenditure kicker effect. But you are so focused on the wrongness of these hacks...</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not a hack sparky that's how they already work. Every Nightmare that actually has a roll attached to it is X-stat +satiety. So your argument is that there would be more mileage out of a hack that does exactly what the game already does. I imagine you can see the problem with expecting anyone to make that argument.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T10:30:03-08:00","id":784236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=784203#post784203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say too, you might have gotten more mileage out of your arguments if you had argued that <b>a better hack would be to add the character's current Satiety before any is spent for the Satiety Expenditure kicker effect.</b> But you are so focused on the wrongness of these hacks...</div> </div> </div> </div>If your suggestion for getting more mileage out of an argument is to propose arguing for a hack that is <i>identical to the printed rules</i>, the issue in focus probably does not lie with your opposition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p133 - Systems</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For purposes of the availability of the High Satiety effect and the determination of dice pools, spending Satiety happens after the roll is made.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T12:52:18-08:00","id":784307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781756-a-few-questions-about-nightmares?p=784231#post784231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not a hack sparky that's how they already work. Every Nightmare that actually has a roll attached to it is X-stat +satiety. So your argument is that there would be more mileage out of a hack that does exactly what the game already does. I imagine you can see the problem with expecting anyone to make that argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing this made me laugh at myself for a good 5 minutes. Obviously, there has also been some QC failures in the production of these hacks, namely that I had skimmed over the precise nature of the die rolls seeing only an A+B and thinking to myself that they were the ordinary [Attribute]+[Skill] pools rather than [Attribute]+[Supernatural Advantage/Integritry]. If someone had pointed that out sooner and mentioned in the worst case scenario, that this rather makes for a 30-die dice pool, which seems like alot (except that such pools are attainable), then the true problems of the hack's mechanisms would have been easier for me to see. <br /> <br /> Let us agree then that Hack #2 truly serves no purpose. This being the case, let me make an alteration to Hack #1, namely that the victim contest the roll with the higher of her Resolve or Composure, rather than adding them together. In a worst case scenario for the Beast, his opponent will likewise access a 20-die pool of dice (just as it is now) and at best mortals will only be able to apply 5 dice (status quo ante bellum).<br /> <br /> My goodness. How clumsy...<br /> <br /> Good catch nalak42.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}